cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SteadyHand, please cite it as below."
title: "SteadyHand: rejection cutoffs for myoelectric control with misfire-rate guarantees"
authors:
  - family-names: Nuthalapati
    given-names: Kishore
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-11-05
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/kishoren18-hue/steadyhand"
url: "https://kishoren18-hue.github.io/steadyhand/"
keywords:
  - electromyography
  - myoelectric control
  - prosthetics
  - conformal prediction
  - uncertainty quantification
abstract: >-
  SteadyHand chooses the confidence cutoff in LibEMG's rejection block from a
  target misfire rate. A conformal cutoff keeps a new user's expected misfire
  rate at or below the target; an adaptive cutoff keeps each user's long-run
  misfire rate at the target plus a vanishing term on any data sequence,
  including electrode shift and limb-position changes.
references:
  - type: article
    title: "LibEMG: An Open Source Library to Facilitate the Exploration of Myoelectric Control"
    authors:
